  - **New `## Ownership map`.** The Rust supervisor only forwards the client's socket frames (`socket.rs`) to the JS manager, which speaks CapTP. So chat and debugger state belong to the manager. The `endor tui` client owns the terminal, layout and modes, and only keeps a cache it rebuilds on reconnect.
  - **`## Phased Implementation` re-cut into 8 phases**, with a size table and a mermaid graph. The mermaid fence passes the parse check.

    | Phase | Size | Depends on |
    |---|---|---|
    | 1 Skeleton and chat transcript (#1525, in flight) | M | — |
    | 2 Chat data path | L | 1 |
    | 3 Spaces and per-space themes | M | 2 |
    | 4 Value inspection and forms | L | 2 |
    | 5 XS debugger baseline | L | 2 and `daemon-xs-worker-debugger` |
    | 6 Debugger richness | M | 5 |
    | 7 Durable breakpoints and controller claim | M | 5 |
    | 8 Polish and escape valves | M | 3, 4, 6 |

    Phases 2 to 7 each list acceptance tests. Focus mode and the pending-commands region now sit in Phase 1, because #1525 already builds them.
  - **New `## Open questions`** (see below), and Known Gaps entries now point to the phases that close them.
